.TH GPUTOP 1 "2026-10-13" "gputop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gputop \- btop-style terminal monitor for AMD Radeon GPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gputop
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads what the amdgpu kernel driver already publishes \(utilisation, clocks,
temperatures, power, throttle reasons, per-process engine time and memory\)
and shows it in one screen. Never writes to the GPU.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Config file instead of the default search locations.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Sampling interval, overriding general.interval_ms.
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\fR
One JSON snapshot to stdout and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-devices\fR
List discovered GPUs as JSON and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Report which metrics this machine can provide, and why any are missing.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR \fIPATH\fR
Record the session (.csv or .json; + .zst compresses).
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/gputop/gputop.toml
.RS
User configuration (see gputop.example.toml).
.RE
.I ~/.config/gputop/config.toml
.RS
Session state written by gputop itself ($GPUTOP_STATE overrides).
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 3
No AMD GPU present.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR radeontop (1)
.SH LICENSE
GPL-3.0-or-later.
